/**
 * ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The real Event Horizon mark, inlined.
 *
 * A 320x320 RGBA PNG of the brand artwork, box-downsampled from the 1254px
 * original with premultiplied alpha so the glow fades out cleanly instead of
 * picking up a dark fringe at the edge.
 *
 * ─── WHY A DATA URI AND NOT A FILE ─────────────────────────────────────
 * The extension's UI renders inside Vortex's own window, so a relative `src`
 * resolves against Vortex's document, not against our folder. Building an
 * absolute `file://` from `__dirname` would work until the dist layout moved,
 * and its failure mode is the worst kind available: a silently broken image
 * where the logo should be, on a machine nobody can inspect.
 *
 * A data URI cannot fail to resolve. That is the trade this project has
 * already made everywhere else — reliability over bytes.
 *
 * GENERATED, not hand-written. To replace the artwork, re-run the downsample
 * against the new source rather than editing this string.
 * ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 */

